{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-429", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/429", "wordCount": 3130, "segments": [{"start": 7.0, "text": "Hello, my name is Davide and"}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "I am an engineer on the"}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "Debugging Technologies Team at"}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "Apple."}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "I'm here with my colleague"}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "Jonas."}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "You might be familiar with po, a"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "way to print variables in LLDB."}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "Today, we will talk about it and"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "how it works."}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "We will also present other ways"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "to look at the variables in your"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "source code together with"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "powerful mechanisms to format"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "the output."}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "LLDB is the debugger that powers"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "the variable view in Xcode."}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "You can see the variables you"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "define and their types there."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "While debugging in Xcode, you"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "can also directly send commands"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "and interact with LLDB through"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "the console in the bottom right"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "of the window."}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "This includes the ability to"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "print the values of the"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "variables to defining your"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "source code while you're"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "investigating a bug in your"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "LLDB offer several ways to"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "accomplish this task."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "Each of which comes with a"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "different set of trade-offs."}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "Let's look at them."}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "As an example, suppose we have a"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "struct that represents a Trip,"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "consisting of a name and a list"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "of destinations."}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "Let's go on a cruise around the"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "Mediterranean."}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "The first command we are going"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "to explore is po, which you can"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "think as of standing for print"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "object description."}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "When we use this command, what"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "we get in return is the object"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "description which is a textual"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "representation of an instance of"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "your type."}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "The system runtime provides a"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "default one but it's possible to"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "customize it."}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "We can do this by adding a"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "conformance to the"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "CustomDebugStringConvertible"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "protocol. This requires having a single"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "property called the"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "debugDescription."}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "Now, if we print the object"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "description in the debugger,"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "we'll see the description we"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "provided instead of the default"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "one."}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "The change only affects the"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "top-level description."}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "If you need to modify the"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "substructure, check the"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "documentation for the"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "CustomerReflectable protocol."}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "This can also be done for"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "Objective-C objects by"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "implementing the description"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "method."}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "But po does more than just print"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "variables."}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "For example, you can take the"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "name of our cruise and compute"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "an uppercase version of it or"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "get an alphabetically sorted"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "array of the cruise"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "destinations."}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "In general, it can evaluate"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "arbitrary expressions."}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "So, anything that would compile"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "at a given prompt in the program"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "can be passed as an argument to"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "the comment."}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "In fact, po is actually an alias"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "for a command called expression"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "with an argument for printing"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "the object description."}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "LECC and LLDB are a convenient"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "way to save keystrokes."}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "If you wanted to implement po"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "yourself, for example, you could"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "use command alias."}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "Specify your own command name as"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "the first argument, and then"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "follow with the command you want"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "to alias."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "Once that's defined, you can use"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "it like any other commands in"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "LLDB."}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "Now that we know what po can do,"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "let's take a deeper look at how"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "it works."}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "Let's go through the steps that"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "po has to perform to deliver a"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "value."}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "To provide the full expressivity"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "of the language you are using"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "LLDB doesn't parse and evaluate"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "the expression itself."}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "Instead, it starts by generating"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "a piece of source code that can"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "be compiled from the expression"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "you gave it, similar to the"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "snippet shown here."}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "Then it uses the embedded Swift"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "and claim compilers to compile"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "the code which gets executed in"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "the context of your debugged"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "program."}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "Once the execution is complete,"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "LLDB has to access the resulting"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "value."}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "From there you need to get the"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "object description."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "To do this, LLDB wraps the"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "previous result in another piece"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "of source code."}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "This also gets compiled and"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "executed in the context of your"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "debug process."}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "The result of this execution is"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "a string that LLDB will display"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "as the result of the po command."}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "Po is only the first of the"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "three ways we are presenting to"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "print variables in LLDB."}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "Let's look at the others."}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "The second way to print"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "variables in an LLDB is the"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "p-command."}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "You can think of it as print"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "without the object description."}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "Let's look at its output."}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "The first thing to notice is"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "that the representation is"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "slightly different from the one"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "provided by po, but it is"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "equivalent in that it contains"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "the same information."}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "The second thing to notice is"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "that the resulting value has"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "been given a name, $R0."}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "This is a special convention in"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "LLDB."}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "The result of each expression is"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "given an incrementing name, such"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "as $R1 and $R2."}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "And this name can be used in"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "later expressions in LLDB."}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "You can refer to $R0 the same"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "way as any other variable in"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "your project."}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "You can, for example, print the"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "fields of destruction."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "Similar to po, p is not a"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "first-class command in LLDB."}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "It's just an alias for the"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "expression command, but without"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "the -- object description after"}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "it. As we previously did with po,"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "let's look at how po works under"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "the hood."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "Since p doesn't have to get the"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "description, it doesn't have to"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "do as much work."}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "You may recall this diagram from"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "the earlier description of po."}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "In fact, the first part"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "compiling and evaluating the"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "expression is exactly the same"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "for both commands."}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "But once it gets the results"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "LLDB perform a step name dynamic"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "type resolution on it."}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "Let's describe it with more"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "details."}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "In order to do that, we have to"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "modify our code example a bit."}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "Let's see how."}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "We change our Trip struct to"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "conform to a protocol name"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "activity."}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "In Swift, the static"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "representation of a type in the"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "source code and the dynamic type"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "at the runtime, aren't"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "necessarily the same."}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "For example, a variable might be"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "declared using a protocol of"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "this type."}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "In this example, the static type"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "of cruise's Activity."}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "But at runtime, the variable"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "will have an instance of type"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "Trip which is the dynamic time."}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "If we print the value of cruise,"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "we get back an object of type"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "Trip because LLDB retell results"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "metadata to display the most"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "accurate type for a given"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "variable at a given program"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "point. This is what we call dynamic"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "type resolution."}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "With the p-command, dynamic type"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "resolution is only performed on"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "the result of the expression."}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "Let's say we want to access one"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "of the field of cruise."}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "When LLDB tries to evaluate this"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "expression through p, it sees"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "that cruise is an object of type"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "Activity and doesn't have a"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "member called name."}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "The evaluation fails with an"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "error."}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "This happens because if you"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "remember, LLDB compiles code"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "where running p and the only"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "type it sees is the one in your"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "source code, the static one."}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "It's the same thing as typing"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "the expression cruise.name in"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "your source code."}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "The static compiler will reject"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "it with an error."}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "If you want to evaluate the"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "expression without errors, you"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "need to first cast the object"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "explicitly to its dynamic type"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "and then access the field on the"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "result."}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "This is true both for the"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "debugger and your source code."}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "P is not yet done with its work."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "After it performed dynamic type"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "resolution on the result, LLDB"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "passes the resulting object to"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "the formatter subsystem which is"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "the part of LLDB responsible for"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "printing a human readable"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "description of objects."}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "Let's dive into it."}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "To show how formatters work,"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "we're going to display their"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "input and output."}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "Here's what that string looks"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "like if there was no formatter"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "for the type."}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "If you want to try yourself, you"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "can pass the -- raw option to p."}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "Standard library types even"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "simple ones like strings and"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "integers have complex"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "representation because they are"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "highly optimized for speed and"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "size."}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "After the formatter operates in"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "it a string looks exactly as you"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "expect, a sequence of"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "characters."}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "LLDB knows about a bunch of"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "commonly used types and provides"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "formatters for them."}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "You can also write for customize"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "formatters."}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "We'll talk about it shortly."}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "We talk about p and po."}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "We are now going to describe the"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "third way to print variables in"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "LLDB, the v-command."}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "The output of v is exactly the"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "same as p as it also relies on"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "the formatter we just described."}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "As with the other two commands,"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "v is just an alias we introduced"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "in Xcode 10.2 for the frame"}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "variable command."}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "Unlike the other two mechanisms,"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "the v-command doesn't compile"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "and execute code at all which"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "makes it very fast."}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "Since v is not compiling code,"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "it does its own syntax which"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "will not necessarily be the same"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "as the language you are"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "debugging."}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "For example, it used the dot and"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "subscript operators to access"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "fields over time."}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "But it won't perform overload"}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "the resolution and computed"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "properties cannot be evaluated"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "since that would require code to"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "be executed."}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "You can use p or po if you need"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "those."}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "As you can guess, v works fairly"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "differently from the other two"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "mechanisms for printing"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "variables."}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "Let's go ahead and clarify some"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "details."}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "In our grand tradition of"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "diagrams here is one for v."}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "We want to print a variable."}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "To do so, v first consults the"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "program state to locate the"}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "variable in memory."}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "Then it reads the value of the"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "variable from memory."}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "Then it performs dynamic type"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "resolution on it."}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "If the user asked to access"}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "subfields, it repeats the step"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "for each of the subfields"}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "performing dynamic type"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "resolution at each round."}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "Once it's done, it passes the"}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "result to the data formatter"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "subsystem."}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "The fact that v performs dynamic"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "type resolution potentially"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "multiple times is an important"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "detail to remember and the big"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "difference in the way p and v"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "operates."}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "The formatter indeed performs"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "dynamic type resolution only"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "once. Let's look at the scenario where"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "these matters."}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "We are back to our example where"}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "p was failing to access the"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "member of cruise."}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "By performing dynamic type"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "resolution at each step of the"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "interpretation, v is able to"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "understand that cruise is an"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "object of type Trip and access"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "its field in memory."}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "This is a scenario where v is"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "strictly more powerful than p"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "and allows you to look at your"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "types where p doesn't or without"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "an explicit cast."}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "We are done describing the three"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "different ways for printing"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "variables in LLDB."}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "Let's have a recap and the"}, {"start": 684.0, "text": "side-by-side comparison of how"}, {"start": 687.0, "text": "the po, p and v commands differ."}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "The first point we want to make"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "is about how objects are"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "presented."}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "The po command uses the object"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "description, whereas the p and v"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "commands use the data formatters"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "to display the object."}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "We also want to remember how our"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "results are computed."}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "Both po and p compile"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "expressions and have access to"}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "the full language."}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "V instead has its own syntax"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "interprets the expression and"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "performs dynamic type resolution"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "for each step of the"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "interpretation."}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "We mentioned earlier that LLDB"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "formatting can be customized."}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "To talk more about that, here is"}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "my colleague Jonas."}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "Hi, I'm Jonas, and I'm also"}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "an engineer on the Debugging"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "Technologies Team."}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "In LLDB, data formatter is"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "defined how variables are"}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "displayed in the debugger."}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "There are building formatters"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "for common types."}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "For instance, when using the"}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "v-commands, we can print the"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "destinations of our cruise and"}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "the array elements are displayed"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "in a readable format."}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "Usually, the default formatter"}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "works great for both the user"}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "defined types and for types"}, {"start": 759.0, "text": "coming from the standard"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "library."}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "But sometimes you might want to"}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "tweak an existing formatter or"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "to find one yourself."}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "And you can, because data"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "formatters in LLDB are fully"}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "extensible."}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "Every type can have its own"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "representation."}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "To help you customize that"}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "representation, LLDB offers"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "filters, summaries and synthetic"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "children."}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "Filters are used to limit the"}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "output of existing formatters."}, {"start": 788.0, "text": "Right now, our Trip only has a"}, {"start": 789.0, "text": "few destinations but as the"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "number increases, the output"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "could become cluttered."}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "By adding a filter, we can"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "specify that we only want to see"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "the Trips name."}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "This not only affects the output"}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "of the formatter in the console,"}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "but also the variables here in"}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "Xcode."}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "Let's remove the filter again"}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "before moving on."}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "Summaries provide a string"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "representation of a type."}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "To give information about that"}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "type at a glance, their data"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "formatter equivalent of the"}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "description that you would"}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "implement for use with po."}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "As with filters, they also"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "affect the variables view in"}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "Xcode."}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "While the members of our Trip"}, {"start": 827.0, "text": "all have summaries, the Trip"}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "itself does not."}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "Let's change that."}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "A good summary would be the"}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "first and last destination."}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "The summary string can contain"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "regular text and special"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "variables that access fields of"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "the time being printed."}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "These variables start with a"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "dollar sign and are wrapped in"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "curly braces."}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "They use the same syntax as the"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "v-commands."}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "The current type for which the"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "summary is defined is access as"}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "var."}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "The summary uses var.name to"}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "access the Trips name and"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "var.destinations to access its"}, {"start": 860.0, "text": "destinations."}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "But there's a problem with the"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "summary."}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "It only works for Trips that"}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "contain exactly three"}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "destinations."}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "Because formatters can't access"}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "computed variables like the"}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "count of an array, we have to"}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "hard-code the index of the last"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "element."}, {"start": 876.0, "text": "Fortunately, there's another"}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "powerful tool available to us."}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "We can also define summaries in"}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "Python."}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "Python formatters can do"}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "arbitrary computations and they"}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "have full access to LLDB's"}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "scripting bridge API which"}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "provides several objects for"}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "accessing the state of the"}, {"start": 893.0, "text": "current debug session."}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "The target is the program that's"}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "currently being debugged."}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "The process, thread, and frame"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "provides access to the"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "corresponding runtime"}, {"start": 904.0, "text": "information."}, {"start": 906.0, "text": "Values of variables, registers,"}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "or expressions are represented"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "by the SB value class."}, {"start": 913.0, "text": "These are particularly"}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "interesting to the data"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "formatters because they are used"}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "to navigate types and their"}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "values."}, {"start": 920.0, "text": "Check out the online"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "documentation for more details."}, {"start": 925.0, "text": "Starting with Xcode 11,"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "scripting uses Python 3."}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "If you have existing Python 2"}, {"start": 930.0, "text": "scripts, check out the Xcode"}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "release notes for more"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "information on transitioning to"}, {"start": 934.0, "text": "Python 3."}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "Let's explore the LLDB API."}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "Executing the script commands"}, {"start": 942.0, "text": "drops this into an interactive"}, {"start": 943.0, "text": "Python interpreter."}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "The current frame is accessible"}, {"start": 947.0, "text": "to the lldb.frame variable."}, {"start": 950.0, "text": "This returns an SBFrame"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "instance."}, {"start": 952.0, "text": "We know that the current frame"}, {"start": 953.0, "text": "contains a variable named"}, {"start": 954.0, "text": "cruise."}, {"start": 956.0, "text": "So, we can go ahead and use find"}, {"start": 958.0, "text": "variable to obtain its SB value."}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "Since these objects power the"}, {"start": 962.0, "text": "data formatters under the hood,"}, {"start": 964.0, "text": "it is no surprise that printing"}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "them looks identical to the"}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "corresponding data formatter"}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "outputs."}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "We also know that cruise has"}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "member named destinations."}, {"start": 974.0, "text": "We can access it by calling"}, {"start": 976.0, "text": "GetChildMemberWithName."}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "The result is another SB value"}, {"start": 980.0, "text": "that represents the destinations"}, {"start": 982.0, "text": "array."}, {"start": 983.0, "text": "Let's try to mimic our earlier"}, {"start": 985.0, "text": "formatter using Python, this"}, {"start": 988.0, "text": "time without hard coding the"}, {"start": 989.0, "text": "index of the last element."}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "We can use GetNumChildren on the"}, {"start": 993.0, "text": "destinations SB value to get the"}, {"start": 995.0, "text": "number of elements."}, {"start": 996.0, "text": "With GetChildAtIndex, we can"}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "access the first element and the"}, {"start": 1000.0, "text": "last element."}, {"start": 1002.0, "text": "Notice that the printed values"}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "are context sensitive."}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "They contain the index in the"}, {"start": 1006.0, "text": "array."}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "SB value instances maintain the"}, {"start": 1009.0, "text": "context of their parent"}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "relation."}, {"start": 1012.0, "text": "Now, we can put everything"}, {"start": 1013.0, "text": "together in a single string."}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "The results, however, it's not"}, {"start": 1017.0, "text": "exactly what we want, by"}, {"start": 1019.0, "text": "printing, begin and end, we get"}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "descriptions of the SB value"}, {"start": 1023.0, "text": "objects."}, {"start": 1024.0, "text": "What we really want here are"}, {"start": 1025.0, "text": "their summaries."}, {"start": 1027.0, "text": "We can use GetSummary to"}, {"start": 1028.0, "text": "retrieve the formatted value and"}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "use that instead."}, {"start": 1032.0, "text": "Now, the result is place only"}, {"start": 1033.0, "text": "the destination strings"}, {"start": 1034.0, "text": "themselves."}, {"start": 1035.0, "text": "Let's put everything together."}, {"start": 1038.0, "text": "Formatters can be defined"}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "directly in the debugger console"}, {"start": 1042.0, "text": "or you can use a file and load"}, {"start": 1043.0, "text": "it into LLDB."}, {"start": 1045.0, "text": "In this case, we'll create a"}, {"start": 1046.0, "text": "file called Trip.py."}, {"start": 1048.0, "text": "When defining a provider in a"}, {"start": 1050.0, "text": "file instead of using the"}, {"start": 1051.0, "text": "current frame to access the"}, {"start": 1052.0, "text": "variable we want to display the"}, {"start": 1054.0, "text": "SB value is passed as an input"}, {"start": 1056.0, "text": "parameter to a function."}, {"start": 1058.0, "text": "The rest of the implementation"}, {"start": 1060.0, "text": "is pretty much identical to what"}, {"start": 1061.0, "text": "we did before."}, {"start": 1063.0, "text": "Another advantage of using"}, {"start": 1064.0, "text": "Python to define the formatter"}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "is that we have control flow."}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "If the trip has no destinations,"}, {"start": 1070.0, "text": "we can just sprint that it's an"}, {"start": 1071.0, "text": "empty trip."}, {"start": 1073.0, "text": "We get the summary for the first"}, {"start": 1074.0, "text": "and last destination and return"}, {"start": 1076.0, "text": "to summary string."}, {"start": 1078.0, "text": "Now, we need to load our new"}, {"start": 1080.0, "text": "summary provider into LLDB."}, {"start": 1082.0, "text": "This is done using the command"}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "script import command."}, {"start": 1086.0, "text": "Next, we need to specify that"}, {"start": 1088.0, "text": "our new formatter is the one to"}, {"start": 1089.0, "text": "use for the Trip type."}, {"start": 1091.0, "text": "Using type summary add and"}, {"start": 1093.0, "text": "providing the type to be"}, {"start": 1094.0, "text": "formatted, and the provider"}, {"start": 1095.0, "text": "function to use."}, {"start": 1097.0, "text": "It's important to use the fully"}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "qualified type here."}, {"start": 1100.0, "text": "With everything hooked up v now"}, {"start": 1102.0, "text": "uses the Python summary provider"}, {"start": 1104.0, "text": "to print a cruise object."}, {"start": 1107.0, "text": "Not only does the summary show"}, {"start": 1108.0, "text": "up in the console, it is also"}, {"start": 1109.0, "text": "displayed in Xcode's Variable"}, {"start": 1111.0, "text": "View."}, {"start": 1112.0, "text": "We've talked about filters and"}, {"start": 1114.0, "text": "summaries."}, {"start": 1115.0, "text": "The final way to customize the"}, {"start": 1116.0, "text": "display of your type is with"}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "synthetic children."}, {"start": 1119.0, "text": "These make it possible to"}, {"start": 1121.0, "text": "customize what kind of children"}, {"start": 1122.0, "text": "your type exposes, such as when"}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "you expend to type in the"}, {"start": 1125.0, "text": "variables view in Xcode."}, {"start": 1128.0, "text": "In Python, each child has an SB"}, {"start": 1129.0, "text": "value, and each can have its own"}, {"start": 1131.0, "text": "summary."}, {"start": 1134.0, "text": "Defining your own synthetic"}, {"start": 1135.0, "text": "child provider is similar to"}, {"start": 1137.0, "text": "defining a summary provider."}, {"start": 1139.0, "text": "But instead of a function you"}, {"start": 1140.0, "text": "define a class that implements"}, {"start": 1141.0, "text": "certain methods."}, {"start": 1143.0, "text": "In addition to init, you provide"}, {"start": 1145.0, "text": "a method to get the total number"}, {"start": 1146.0, "text": "of children, the synthetic"}, {"start": 1148.0, "text": "children themselves, and an"}, {"start": 1149.0, "text": "index for a given name."}, {"start": 1151.0, "text": "A full example of this is"}, {"start": 1152.0, "text": "available in the resources link"}, {"start": 1154.0, "text": "from this session."}, {"start": 1157.0, "text": "Just like before, use command"}, {"start": 1159.0, "text": "script import to load the Python"}, {"start": 1161.0, "text": "source code into LLDB."}, {"start": 1163.0, "text": "In this case, we already loaded"}, {"start": 1164.0, "text": "this file earlier and running"}, {"start": 1166.0, "text": "the command again will reload"}, {"start": 1167.0, "text": "the file."}, {"start": 1169.0, "text": "To specify the formatter, to use"}, {"start": 1171.0, "text": "for synthetic children use type"}, {"start": 1173.0, "text": "synthetic add and provide the"}, {"start": 1175.0, "text": "type to be formatted and the"}, {"start": 1176.0, "text": "class to use."}, {"start": 1179.0, "text": "After going through the effort"}, {"start": 1180.0, "text": "of defining our own custom"}, {"start": 1182.0, "text": "providers, we don't want to lose"}, {"start": 1183.0, "text": "them at the end of our debug"}, {"start": 1185.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 1186.0, "text": "Any command you type in the"}, {"start": 1187.0, "text": "console can be persisted in the"}, {"start": 1189.0, "text": ".lldbinit file in your home"}, {"start": 1191.0, "text": "directory."}, {"start": 1192.0, "text": "This file gets automatically"}, {"start": 1193.0, "text": "loaded at the beginning of your"}, {"start": 1195.0, "text": "debug session."}, {"start": 1198.0, "text": "LLDB has a variety of features"}, {"start": 1200.0, "text": "to help you see the state of"}, {"start": 1202.0, "text": "your program while debugging."}, {"start": 1203.0, "text": "Use v, p, or po to print"}, {"start": 1206.0, "text": "variables, depending on whether"}, {"start": 1208.0, "text": "you just need to display its"}, {"start": 1209.0, "text": "value, execute code or get the"}, {"start": 1211.0, "text": "object description."}, {"start": 1213.0, "text": "Customize or define your own"}, {"start": 1214.0, "text": "data formatters, using filters,"}, {"start": 1217.0, "text": "string summaries, and synthetic"}, {"start": 1218.0, "text": "children."}, {"start": 1219.0, "text": "Finally, if you have scripts"}, {"start": 1221.0, "text": "written in Python 2, update them"}, {"start": 1223.0, "text": "to be compatible with Python 3."}, {"start": 1225.0, "text": "The version used by LLDB"}, {"start": 1227.0, "text": "starting in Xcode 11."}, {"start": 1230.0, "text": "For more information, check out"}, {"start": 1232.0, "text": "the page for this session on"}]}
